# Sprinklr channel recognition — CALL vs EMAIL

**Chat scope:** Email processing agent. Use before treating an open Fall as an email RE/PR case.

**Reference snapshot (call):** Fall **#57114650** (Uwe Kommer), 2026-09-05  
Artifacts: `.cursor/reports/sprinklr-call-overlay-2026-09-05.png`, `sprinklr-call-overlay-dom-2026-09-05.json`, `sprinklr-call-vs-email-selectors-2026-09-05.json`, `CALL-VS-EMAIL-RECOGNITION-2026-09-05.md`

---

## Hard rule

If the visible case is a **CALL** (voice), do **not** run the normal email RE → PR → LF email path as if it were Care Webform email.

- Do **not** draft a customer email reply for a live/disposition call unless the user explicitly asks.
- Prefer: identify channel → ask user / skip / document only.

---

## CALL markers (any strong set → treat as CALL)

### A) Live / voice overlays (strongest)

Visible UI widgets (bottom of Care Console):

| Marker | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| **Im Gespräch** | Agent in call status (timer, e.g. `08:26`) |
| **Mikrofon angeschlossen** | Mic connected |
| **VOIP Nailed Up Leitung: Verbunden** (or similar VOIP line status) | Voice path up |
| **Medienauslagerung fehlgeschlagen** (optional warning) | Media offload status on call UI |
| Floating **Case #…** widget with **o2 Disposition Plan** / **Disposition Codes** / Next | Call disposition overlay |
| Green **phone handset** icon next to MSISDN in disposition card | Voice contact |

### B) Timeline / conversation (strong)

| Marker | Example |
|--------|---------|
| **Eingehender Anruf** | Incoming call thread title |
| Timeline labels **Anruf** | Call events |
| **Anruf beendet – X Mins Y Sekunden** | Call ended duration |
| **Aufzeichnung gestartet** / recording UI | Call recording |
| **Anruf wurde getrennt** / TIMEOUT | Disconnect events |
| Audio bubbles / waveforms (`0:09`, `3:57`, play bars) | Not email body text |
| DOM testids (when present) | `audio_pres`, `call-button`, `omniMedia`, `mediaItems`, `mediaList-OMNI_TEMPLATE_*` |

### C) Case Informationen (supporting)

Verified on snapshot Fall #57114650:

| Field | Call example |
|-------|----------------|
| **Quelle** | `Aura Care Shared` (not Care Webform) |
| **Ziel** | e.g. `Sales Beratung - Mobile Pilot 2` |

Quelle/Ziel alone are not enough (queues vary) — combine with A/B.

### D) Negative email signals on a call

| Signal | Call snapshot |
|--------|----------------|
| `[data-testid="html-message-content"]` count | **0** (no classic email HTML bodies) |
| TinyMCE / `body#tinymce` | Often absent during live call |
| `section[aria-label="Nachricht verfassen"]` | May still exist in shell — **do not** treat as proof of email |

---

## EMAIL markers (treat as EMAIL)

| Marker | Notes |
|--------|--------|
| Care Webform / email **Quelle** typical of inbound mail | e.g. Care Webform (not Aura Care Shared call) |
| Visible email thread with **html-message-content** / readable mail bodies | Fan/brand messages with text |
| Subject / Von: / Betreff email structure | Classic mail |
| No **Im Gespräch** / Disposition Plan / Anruf timeline | Absence of call overlays |
| RE extract prints normal **CUSTOMER EMAIL** body text | Not only Anruf/audio events |

---

## Detection order (agent / scripts)

1. If **Im Gespräch** or Disposition Plan overlay visible → **CALL**.
2. Else if timeline has **Eingehender Anruf** / **Anruf beendet** / audio media testids → **CALL**.
3. Else if `html-message-content` present and no call overlays → **EMAIL**.
4. Else if ambiguous → ask user; do not PR an email reply.

Suggested log lines:

- `CHANNEL: CALL`  
- `CHANNEL: EMAIL`  
- `CHANNEL: UNKNOWN — confirm before RE/PR`

---

## Operator note

This rule is for **recognition**. Call handling / disposition codes are out of scope for the email RE/PR/LF pipeline unless explicitly extended later.
